<title>USA: U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory vegoil product use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 1,128.1 million lbs of vegoils in March in edible product output versus a revised 1,286.5 million lbs in February and 1,174.9 in March 1996.</p>
<p>U.S. factory vegoil use with refining losses were as follows:</p>
<p>   (Mln Lbs) --  March 97   Feb 97   March 96</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil   1,125.6   1,005.3   1,064.1</p>
<p> Cottonseed Oil	N/A	N/A	    N/A</p>
<p>Year-to-date oil use with refining losses (Mln Lbs):</p>
<p>				    1997	   1996</p>
<p>		 Soybean Oil   3,251.9	3,022.9</p>
<p>	    Cottonseed Oil	 N/A	    N/A</p>
<p> OUTPUT -- Soybean Crude   3,930.2	3,888.9</p>
<p>		     Refined   2,955.5	2,956.9</p>
<p>	  Cottonseed Crude     353.3	  485.6</p>
<p>		     Refined     245.0	  266.1</p>
<p>		  Corn Crude     553.3	  506.4</p>
<p>		     Refined     209.7	  255.4</p>
</text>
